\]

This relation is not exact—the precise value depends on the specific initial conditions and the nature of the forcing. But the scaling is universal: the exponent is of order \( 1/\mathcal{G}_c \).

This provides a **testable prediction**: the critical exponent of the Navier-Stokes blow-up should be approximately \( 3/e \). If numerical simulations or rigorous proofs yield a different value, the gap theory is falsified.

